        <div class="faq-accordion">
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary class="faq-question">How does Washington State's tiered Real Estate Excise Tax (REET) work when selling?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Washington State levies a tiered REET on property sales. Portions of the sale price are taxed progressively: 1.1% on amounts up to $525,000; 1.28% on portion between $525,000 and $1,525,000; 2.75% on portion between $1,525,000 and $3,025,000; and 3.0% on portion over $3,025,000 (plus local municipal surtaxes). You can model your exact WA REET breakdown using my <a href="/sellerproceeds/" style="color: var(--card-accent-color); font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">Seller Net Proceeds Calculator</a>.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary class="faq-question">How does pre-listing prep funding work with Notable?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Notable allows homeowners to access up to $50,000 in zero-upfront-cost funding for repairs, painting, landscaping, and staging. Qualifying requires a 680+ credit score and at least 20% home equity. Vendors are paid directly, and you repay the funds out of your escrow proceeds when the home sells. Learn more on our <a href="/resources/notable/" style="color: var(--card-accent-color); font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">Notable Resource Guide</a>.
                </div>
            </details>

